## 2026-10-24 — save-grace versus break-skip source audit

- The apparent three-use allowance belongs to Mac desktop's BlueCloud save-unlock reservation (`grantOneTimeSaveUnlock`): at most three grants per day, one grant in the current break, with a 4-minute default. The break window is hidden during that allowance. `skipBreak()` has class/strict-lock guards and no three-use counter.
- Windows source +113 has a separate device-local save grace: two-minute default, at most once per rolling hour. Its break-skip path has class/strict-lock guards and no three-use counter. The two save policies therefore do not share one quota contract today.
- Windows +114 source work makes the existing grace countdown visible in compact mode, avoids full-screen animated radial repaint, prevents lock-policy reconciliation during the grace, and checks actual native hook-release results before reporting success. Source/build evidence does not establish paired live acceptance; Mac installed1.0.36 and Windows installed0.2.9+108 remain distinct from candidates.


