## 2026-11-04 — `pomodoro_account_settings_retention_v1` / `cross_device_absolute_countdown_v1` (pending)

- Capability IDs: `pomodoro_account_settings_retention_v1`; `cross_device_absolute_countdown_v1`.
- Expected behavior: the same BlueCloud account restores the latest Vintage Pomodoro settings after login/reinstall, retains them through at most 90 days since last Pomodoro use, deletes the settings snapshot after that interval, and rejects stale offline copies. Mac and Windows show the same absolute timer deadline and countdown. Confirmed wake starts the configured 120-minute protection interval.
- Mac implementation: account snapshot carries `pomodoroLastUsedAt`; V2 login pull recognizes `snapshotExpiredAt`, blocks the legacy stale fallback, and does not republish a local snapshot whose last use predates expiry. Break overlay uses the corrected clock and main-process remaining duration. Source and signed candidate are in the canonical Mac checkout.
- Windows implementation/source: current canonical `C:\Users\delig\Desktop\app dev\timer1` and installed UI have not been inspected this turn; do not treat prior heartbeat telemetry as visible runtime proof.
- Shared contract: use account `cloudUserId`; timestamps are epoch milliseconds for `pomodoroLastUsedAt` and ISO-8601 for `snapshotExpiredAt`; reject missing/old use markers after expiry; a new explicit Pomodoro use permits a new snapshot. Expired settings are removed while diagnostics event retention remains three days.
- Lifecycle: `pending` until Brainwire production deploy/read-after-write, Mac signed candidate installation and login restore, offline/restart durability, and Windows-source/installed-receiver bidirectional timer and settings parity are verified. The local wake setting reads enabled at 120 minutes, but current wake state is complete, so live wake behavior remains pending.
- Evidence: `work/task-proof/pomodoro-settings-retention-parity-20261104.txt`; server boundary tests pass, Mac full source check/build/signature pass; no production deploy, Mac install/login journey, or Windows UI journey yet.

### 2026-11-04 follow-up — legacy bridge and actual use marker

Mac records the corrected `pomodoroLastUsedAt` when a user saves timer settings as well as when they start/resume a timer. The Brainwire legacy `/api/cloud-state/pomodoroCloud` route clears legacy snapshot copies when V2 expires, rejects stale/missing-use writes, and bridges a post-expiry fresh-use legacy snapshot into canonical V2. Store, V2 HTTP and legacy HTTP boundary tests pass. Windows must ship a client that records and sends the use marker; its current source/installed behavior remains unverified, so capability status stays `pending`.
